p.src:
We can formalize the rule with the notation already in hand: $\begin{aligned}
B_A &= \text{the payoff the audience cares about},\\
R_A &= \text{the evidence that this payoff can actually be delivered}.\end{aligned}$ The novice entrepreneur often wants to start with $R_A$: the algorithm, the patent, the founders, the brilliance of the vision, the claim to be visionary. Jones is not denying that such things matter. He is saying that they matter only if they give the listener a reason to believe the benefit.

