p.src:
Jones reduces the situation to two large questions: $\begin{aligned}
Q_{\text{inv}}^{(1)} &= \text{How will you make money?},\\
Q_{\text{inv}}^{(2)} &= \text{How will I make money?}\end{aligned}$ Everything else is subordinate. Under $Q_{\text{inv}}^{(1)}$ sit the familiar business questions: what is broken, why is the solution better, are customers emerging, who is on the team, how will sales happen, what about manufacturing, what about IP? Under $Q_{\text{inv}}^{(2)}$ sit terms, ownership, exit, and return.

